WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.100
Most AI didn't come
through the front door.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.025
It came as a vendor pilot,
a key in a config file,

3
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:08.425
or a feature switched on in
software you already had.

4
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:13.321
So it arrived without what an employee's
account gets automatically: an owner,

5
00:00:13.321 --> 00:00:17.987
a place in the organization, a governed
credential, reviews and an end date.

6
00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:20.463
The good news is you
don't need new controls.

7
00:00:20.463 --> 00:00:24.035
The account, identifier,
authenticator and least-privilege

8
00:00:24.035 --> 00:00:27.537
controls you already meet apply
to non-person accounts too.

9
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:29.413
The real gap is coverage.

10
00:00:29.413 --> 00:00:34.313
The AI's account just isn't in the
inventory those controls are tested against.

11
00:00:34.313 --> 00:00:36.480
Here's what closing that gap looks like.
